1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,504
A person throws a stone into the lake and circular ripples form.

2
00:00:04,454 --> 00:00:09,747
The radius of the outer circle grows at a constant rate of one foot per second.

3
00:00:09,747 --> 00:00:15,704
The orange circle is the wave front, and the light-blue layer is the area it encloses.

4
00:00:15,704 --> 00:00:21,928
Use Throw the stone to see the throw, Play to make time move forward, or move the time slider.

5
00:00:21,928 --> 00:00:27,313
Notice that the radius always grows at the same pace, but the area does not.

6
00:00:27,313 --> 00:00:32,752
On the area graph, the slope of the tangent is the rate at which the area grows.

7
00:00:32,752 --> 00:00:37,194
With Go to r equals four feet you reach the instant of the problem.

8
00:00:37,194 --> 00:00:41,489
The panel keeps that rate hidden until you turn on Reveal answer.

